<mxCell id="storage" value="DATA\n\nPostGIS\nElasticsearch\nRedis Geo\nS3 (images)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1bee7;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="195" width="220" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="principles" value="KEY DESIGN RULES\n\n1. Bounding box + Haversine pattern: Cheap lat/lng BETWEEN filter gets 10K candidates from 10M rows via B-tree index in ~5ms. Then Haversine formula on those 10K only (exact circle) in ~5ms. Total: &lt;10ms vs 1000ms without index.\n\n2. Spatial index choice: QuadTree (in-memory, &lt;1M pts, &lt;1ms), Geohash (any SQL, shard-friendly, ~50ms), PostGIS GIST (complex shapes, ACID, ~100ms), Elasticsearch BKD tree (billions, ~50ms), Redis GEORADIUS (real-time updates, &lt;5ms).\n\n3. Geohash edge case: Two points 50m apart on cell boundary have different prefixes. Query 9 cells (center + 8 neighbors) then Haversine post-filter for exact circle.\n\n4. Hybrid architecture: Redis hot cache (top 1000 per city, &lt;5ms, 80% hits) → Elasticsearch (search + filters, ~50ms, 95%) → PostgreSQL PostGIS (source of truth, ~100ms, 5%).\n\n5. Geographic sharding: Shard by region with 10km overlap buffers. Small radius (&lt;10km) = 1 shard. Large radius (&gt;50km) = scatter-gather 3-5 shards + merge-sort.\n\n6. Real-time vs static: Uber drivers → Redis GEOADD every 5s (upsert). Restaurants → PostgreSQL primary, batch sync to ES every 5 min." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="350" y="420" width="930" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="user" value="USER\n\nSearches POIs\nFilters, sorts\nViews details\nWrites reviews" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#bbdefb;strokeColor=#1976d2;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="50" y="230" width="200" height="125" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
