<mxCell id="analogy" value="BEGINNER ANALOGY: The platform is finding the nearest library branch. Bounding box narrows to your neighborhood (fast, eliminates citywide search). Spatial index (QuadTree/Geohash/GIST) is the card catalog organized by location. Haversine measures exact walking distance. Redis is a sticky note listing top 3 closest branches. Elasticsearch answers 'find nearby libraries open now with meeting rooms' in one query. PostgreSQL PostGIS is the master ledger where every address is permanently recorded." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1f5fe;strokeColor=#0277bd;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="50" y="840" width="1530" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>